Z||000000||SmittyABP||03-15-2001||02:28 AM||||To who is willing to help  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I have just recently purchased an 86 fiero V6 SE with 125,000 miles. I have yet to pick it up, but the previous said this about the car "it has a bad #1 cylinder connecting rod bearing. The motor runs but has a knock." Obviously, I know knocking isnt good. I want to know, how bad is the #1 cylinder connecting rod bearing being bad? And can I actually Drive it? How easy (or hard lol) is it to fix? And in the case that I need a new engine, can i use any V6 2.8 Front wheel drive engine? Please help! I just got this car and i need help!<BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Smitty(ABP)<BR>smitty@illbredabp.com<BR>www.geocities.com/smittyabp||||reg||7
Z||000001||Carrolles||03-15-2001||07:21 AM||||A rod knock is not good at all.  You will probably be able to drive it home if you don't have far to go and you don't push the engine very hard.<P>Repair means basically a complete overhaul.  It would not make sense to go that far into an engine without doing it all.<P>A front drive 2.8 or 3.1 will work but you have to be careful which one you choose.  Do a search for engine swaps for info or contact Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory at  (256) 420-5391  Fierofactory@juno.com<P>The non-fiero 2.8L engines have smaller valves in the heads and I believe have lower compression.  The 3.1L engines come in several varieties and not all work with the Fiero intake.<P>Good luck and welcome to the world of Fieros.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||SmittyABP||03-15-2001||09:11 AM||||Well unfortunently, i DO have far to go...about 300 miles actually from Philly back to ohio, and i dont have the cash to tow it back, so im hopin nothing happens.<P>------------------<BR>Smitty(ABP)<BR>smitty@illbredabp.com<BR>www.geocities.com/smittyabp||||reg||9
